{
  "slug": "aria-knowledge",
  "name": "Aria Knowledge",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "ARIA is automated knowledge capture, management, and application for Claude Code. It actively learns during AI-assisted development sessions — insights, decisions, patterns, gotchas — and promotes validated knowledge into an indexed markdown knowledge base that is proactively applied in sessions and on every edit to improve development and accuracy. It runs in Claude Code, fully local. Core feature sets are:\n\nKnowledge Lifecycle — automatic capture from conversations and pre-compaction transcripts, staging backlogs, review workflows, promotion to tagged files, staleness detection, and archival. A pipeline from raw signal to validated knowledge.\n\nDecision Discipline — hook-enforced impact assessment on every file edit, change framework with scope verification, pre/post edit checks, configurable critical paths, and abbreviated mode for planning docs. Not guidelines — active enforcement.\n\nContextual Retrieval — tag-based indexing with cross-references, on-demand knowledge loading by topic, project tag expansion, entity detection, and session-start surfacing. The right knowledge at the right time.\n\nARIA — Anchored Reasoning and Insight Architecture  — is a human-in-the-loop knowledge kit focused on knowledge refinement and applied reasoning in Claude Code sessions.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **30 skills** and **12 MCP servers**.\n\n- **Skills** (30): `ask` (Research a question, check existing knowledge first, draft a knowledge doc from the answer, and save directly to…), `audit-config` (Audit project configuration and documentation for drift, staleness, and broken references), `audit-knowledge` (Scan Claude memory and plans for extractable knowledge), `audit-share` (Batch-review personal knowledge for promotion to team-shared project knowledge), `backlog` (View and manage pending backlog items), `clip` (Save a URL or text snippet to the knowledge intake for later review), `clip-thread` (Capture a chat or email thread from a connected MCP to the knowledge intake), `codemap` (Generate or update a feature-organized CODEMAP.md for any codebase), and 22 more\n- **MCP servers** (12): `slack`, `ms365`, `gmail`, `linear`, `asana`, `atlassian`, `monday`, `clickup`, and 4 more\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install aria-knowledge@claude-community` from `mikeprasad/aria-knowledge` (`plugin`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 30,
    "mcp": 12
  },
